Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the DualSense's speaker over Bluetooth (TODO 213)

The game hands its sound for the controller's speaker to the runtime (ps2_sony_pad.h: setSpeakerWanted,
submitSpeaker, speakerLive). On a DualSense over Bluetooth the device thread then sends an audio report 0x36
every 10.67 ms: the audio set-up, the pad's state (motors, light bar, player LEDs, trigger effects when they
change, the speaker's volume bytes it needs in every report), an empty haptics block and one 10 ms Opus frame
(200 bytes, constant bit rate) of 512 frames of the game's 48 kHz sound squeezed to 480 - the layout and cadence
of our earlier launcher's stream (its packet format proven by the DS5Dongle project). While it streams the 0x31
reports stop (the state rides the audio reports). A 1024-frame cushion before the first frame; silence while the
game's sound runs dry. 50 refused reports in a row: the stream stops for that connection and the sound stays on
the PC. libopus 1.5.2 (BSD) comes in through FetchContent (Windows).

